implementationPlan.description:
Test row VC-P2 in scripts/tests/local-runner-vm-control.test.mjs (DoD 1, 2). Edit with the Edit tool in your task worktree W (a TOOL witness: no shell write and no subagent edit). Append this test after VC-P1, the file's last test, exactly as in the reference diff /mnt/d/moe-scratch/d3a9-win/intended.diff (dry-run green at 0fa7750e):
```js

test('VC-P2 with no probe injected, a runner alive on this host holds its seat VM through cleanupReport, reconcileReport and runVmControl', async t => {
  const { ledger, names: [name] } = await ledgerWith(t, [{ workerId: 'me', runner: `${process.pid}@x`, host: localRunnerHost() }]); // this process
  const { calls, provider } = fakeProvider({ [name]: 'Running' });
  const daemon = fakeDaemon({ seats: { me: gone('me') } }); // the seat is gone and no lease is held: only the runner probe keeps the VM
  const proof = { ledger, provider: { ...provider, keyDir: scratch(t) }, call: daemon.call };
  const held = [{ instance: name, reason: 'runner-alive' }];
  const cleanup = { schema: 'moe-vm-cleanup-v1', deleted: [], preserved: held, errors: [], invalid: 0 };
  const reconcile = { schema: 'moe-vm-reconcile-v1', reconciled: [], unknown: [], invalid: 0, held, retired: [] };
  assert.deepEqual([await cleanupReport(proof), await reconcileReport(proof)], [cleanup, reconcile]);
  for (const [command, report] of [['cleanup', cleanup], ['reconcile', reconcile]]) {
    const out = await captured([command, '--project', scratch(t)], proof);
    assert.deepEqual([out.code, JSON.parse(out.stdout)], [0, report]);
  }
  assert.deepEqual([calls, daemon.calls, (await ledger.read(name)).phase], [[], [SL, SL, SL, SL], 'owned']); // no provider call, no lease read
});
```
Why each piece:
- The record's runner is this test process: `${process.pid}@x`, the `<pid>@<token>` form runnerProbe parses, on host localRunnerHost(). The ledger stamps platform as process.platform, so the production runnerProbe (signal 0 to this pid) answers true.
- fakeDaemon says the seat is gone and lists no resources, so the lease is free. Only the runner probe can hold the VM.
- No runnerAlive is passed anywhere:
  - cleanupReport and reconcileReport use their `runnerAlive = runnerProbe` default;
  - runVmControl, called through the file's captured() helper with deps ledger, provider and call only, passes `deps.runnerAlive`, which is undefined, so the default applies there too.
- Expected:
  - cleanup preserves the record and reconcile holds it, with reason 'runner-alive', both called directly and as runVmControl's one JSON line (exit 0);
  - the fake provider records NO call at all, so nothing is deleted;
  - the daemon sees exactly four moe.get_seat_liveness calls and never moe.list_resources (the runner check comes before the lease read);
  - the record stays 'owned'.
- keyDir is a scratch dir, so a mutant that purges cannot touch the real key dir.
- On error handling: the row uses the file's own scratch() helper, whose t.after rmSync removes every temp dir on pass and on failure.

Plan-time results:
- 20/20 pass on Linux node 24 (19 at base).
- Under Windows node.exe: 18 pass plus 2 existing skips.
- M28, M29 and M30 (comment-1834b0bb) each fail VC-P2 alone (`ℹ fail 1`).
